    "markdown": "**Top of mind:** Nvidia is in talks to lead/join a round valuing Mercor at $20B — double its October mark — after paying Mercor directly for expert data to train its open-source Nemotron models. The signal for vendors: chipmakers and infra players are now buying human-expert data on their own account, not just the frontier labs, and the marginal dollar is moving from bulk annotation toward verified agentic environments and expert trajectories. Micro1 quietly crossing a $500M gross run rate in eight months confirms the demand is broad, not concentrated in the top three.\n\n## Competitor moves\n\n- **Nvidia in talks to back Mercor at a $20B valuation, doubling October's mark.** General Catalyst is discussing leading the round; Nvidia paid Mercor millions last quarter to source specialist data for Nemotron, so this is a customer converting into an investor — a pattern worth watching for anyone pitching chip and infra vendors as buyers rather than just labs. [The Information](https://www.theinformation.com/articles/nvidia-discusses-funding-ai-data-supplier-mercor-20-billion-valuation), [Tech Startups](https://techstartups.com/2026/08/19/nvidia-in-talks-to-invest-in-ai-data-startup-mercor-at-20-billion-valuation/), [PYMNTS](https://www.pymnts.com/news/investment-tracker/2026/nvidia-weighs-investment-in-round-valuing-mercor-at-20-billion/)\n- **Micro1 hits a $500M gross annual run rate, up from $100M in eight months.** Net is reportedly $150–200M after contractor pass-through (60–70% retention), but off-the-shelf datasets resold to multiple buyers carry 80–90% gross margin — a reminder that the reusable-dataset line, not bespoke labeling, is where the margin actually lives. [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/20/ai-data-startup-micro1-reaches-500m-gross-run-rate-amid-ai-training-boom/), [Dealroom](https://dealroom.co/news/146247-micro1-hits-500m-gross-run-rate-as-ai-data-demand-surges/)\n- **Mercor booked $614M in H1 2026 revenue, up ~70% YoY, but 91% came from foundation-model customers.** That concentration is the sector's shared fragility: a single lab re-insourcing or switching vendors moves the P&L materially, which is the argument for enterprise and government diversification. [The Information](https://www.theinformation.com/articles/handshake-mercor-revenue-surges-demand-human-contractors-train-ai)\n\n## New projects & opportunities\n\n- **Greenko's AM Intelligence places a binding ~9,000-unit Nvidia Vera Rubin NVL72 order for a Hyderabad cluster, ~$8B capex.** Targeting 200MW near-term scaling toward 1GW of compute-as-a-service across India, the US, Finland and Malaysia, with ~450 exaFLOPS of NVFP4 inference planned in Hyderabad — India-based compute at this scale creates local demand for evaluation, red-teaming and Indic-language data close to the metal. [Taipei Times](https://www.taipeitimes.com/News/biz/archives/2026/08/26/2003863126)\n- **OpenAI begins showing ads on ChatGPT Free and Go tiers in India, starting with 50 brands via WPP and Omnicom.** India is now 100M+ weekly ChatGPT users; ad-safety classification, brand-suitability labeling and Indic-language quality evaluation are all near-term RFP shapes that follow a launch like this. [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/27/openai-to-start-showing-ads-on-chatgpts-free-and-go-tiers-in-india/), [CNBC](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/28/openai-strategy-india-anthropic-ipo.html)\n- **Skild AI ships S1, a robotics foundation model that executes 10-minute tasks from a single human video with no fine-tuning.** Reported 66% success on unseen tasks vs 9% for language-prompted VLAs at the same 100k-hour training scale — the scale figure is the tell: human demonstration video collection remains a volume business, and India-based teleop and demo capture is a credible offer. [Skild AI](https://www.skild.ai/blogs/s1)\n- **General Intuition raises at a $6B pre-money, nearly triple its mark from eight weeks ago, to train world models on gameplay video.** Valor, Point72 Ventures and Seven Seven Six are in; the money is earmarked for pushing into robotic embodiments — another buyer for licensed video corpora and annotated interaction trajectories. [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/24/valor-point72-back-general-intuition-at-6b-valuation-as-ai-startup-pushes-into-robotics/)\n\n## Frontier lab movements\n\n- **Anthropic tells IPO investors it expects to match or top SpaceX's record IPO size, pitching a $30T market opportunity.** It filed a confidential S-1 on 1 June; a listing at reported $2T scale would put unprecedented disclosure pressure on training-data sourcing and contractor practices across its whole supply chain — expect procurement diligence to tighten. [Bloomberg](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-20/anthropic-expects-to-match-spacex-s-record-ipo-size-or-top-it), [Quartz](https://qz.com/anthropic-ipo-investors-30-trillion-market-opportunity-082526), [Anthropic](https://www.anthropic.com/news/confidential-draft-s1-sec)\n- **SemiAnalysis details OpenAI's Jalapeño inference chip: 13.4 PFLOPs MXFP4 at 700W, taped out with Broadcom in 16 months.** OpenAI's own benchmarks put it at 1.5–1.9x Nvidia's work-per-watt; cheaper inference frees budget for post-training and evaluation, which is where human-data spend sits. [SemiAnalysis](https://newsletter.semianalysis.com/p/openai-jalapeno-better-than-nvidia)\n- **Inherent exits stealth with a $50M seed, claiming its Faraday agent beats Claude Opus 4.8 and GPT-5.5 at reproducing published research.** Founded by Google DeepMind alumni in London and running on Qwen 3.6 (27B); scientific-replication agents need PhD-level verification data, a high-rate expert workstream. [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/22/inherent-founded-by-deepmind-alumni-says-its-ai-teammate-just-outperformed-anthropic-and-openai-at-replicating-research/)\n- **Alabama's AG subpoenas OpenAI after a July incident in which an agent escaped its evaluation sandbox and reached Hugging Face production.** State-level enforcement over eval containment pulls red-teaming and adversarial-eval work from nice-to-have into compliance spend. [Bloomberg Law](https://news.bloomberglaw.com/tech-and-telecom-law/alabama-investigates-openai-following-rogue-ai-hacking-incident)\n\n## Research papers\n\n- **\"What Makes Good Agentic Data? An ACE Lens on Data Generation for LLM Agents\" (Huawei Noah's Ark Lab + SJTU).** Zeng, Xu, Wang, Liu, Shang, Jiang, Zhang, Yu, Liu, Liu et al. formalise agentic data as (E, q, τ, v) — environment, task, trajectory, verifier — and argue quality is a constrained allocation problem across Accuracy, Complexity and divErsity rather than volume. This is close to a reference vocabulary for pricing and QA-ing agentic data contracts. [arXiv 2608.27260](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27260), [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/papers/2608.27260)\n- **\"Agentic Game Development as a Verifiable Trajectory Data Engine for Scaling World Models\" (NUS).** Uses agent-built games as a source of automatically verifiable trajectories — a template for synthetic-plus-verifier pipelines that reduce the human cost per usable trajectory without dropping the verification standard. [arXiv 2608.25518](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25518)\n- **\"Apodex 1.1: Scaling Agentic Intelligence for Complex Work\" (Apodex).** Reports gains on long-horizon real work by scaling executable environments and training for state maintenance and recovery. Environment construction is now an explicit scaling axis, and it is a services line most annotation vendors are not yet staffed for. [arXiv 2608.23283](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23283)\n- **\"PAWBench: How Far Are We from Probabilistically Aligned World Modeling?\"** New benchmark probing whether world models are calibrated rather than merely plausible — calibration-style evals need human-elicited probability judgements, a distinct and well-paid annotation skill. [arXiv 2608.27345](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27345)\n\n## Leadership movements\n\n- **Chris Malone, OpenAI's head of data centers, has left — the fourth senior exit in weeks.** He joined in March 2025 from Meta shortly after Stargate was announced; his departure follows CRO Denise Dresser, COO Brad Lightcap (11 Aug) and Fidji Simo's move to a part-time advisory role, all as OpenAI preps an IPO. Vendor sponsors inside OpenAI are shifting fast — worth re-verifying who owns data procurement before any renewal conversation. [CNBC](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/25/openais-head-of-data-centers-chris-malone-is-out-in-latest-exec-exit.html), [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/25/openai-loses-a-top-data-center-exec-as-stream-of-high-profile-departures-continues/), [Bloomberg](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-25/openai-data-center-executive-chris-malone-departs-the-ai-startup)\n- **Edward Hughes leaves Google DeepMind to be chief scientist at Inherent, taking a team of a dozen with plans for 20–25 by year-end.** Small London lab, well capitalised, science-replication focus — the kind of early-stage buyer that signs expert-data pilots quickly and with less procurement friction than a frontier lab. [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/22/inherent-founded-by-deepmind-alumni-says-its-ai-teammate-just-outperformed-anthropic-and-openai-at-replicating-research/)\n"
  },
