    "markdown": "**Top of mind:** Reports that Anthropic is targeting a record $2 trillion October IPO — with backers projecting $100–120B annualized revenue by year-end — signal that frontier-lab data budgets should keep expanding into 2027. Meanwhile, Forbes-driven scrutiny of US data vendors (Surge, Mercor, Turing) selling to Chinese labs keeps compliance and neutrality front and center — a differentiation opening for vendors who can prove clean customer books.\n\n## Competitor moves\n\n- **Mercor's H1 2026 revenue tops $614M, up 70% YoY — but ~90% comes from foundation labs like OpenAI.** Confirms the expert-data boom is real, and that extreme customer concentration is the sector's structural risk; labs pulling work in-house would hit hard. Mercor is separately reported at a ~$2B gross annualized run rate. [BigGo Finance](https://finance.biggo.com/news/865c23cb-3e0d-4c21-aa0d-6bf2a7fc8d1a), [The Information](https://www.theinformation.com/articles/handshake-mercor-revenue-surges-demand-human-contractors-train-ai), [Dealroom](https://app.dealroom.co/news/note/mercor-doubles-to-2b-gross-revenue-run-rate-as-ai-labs-buy-expert-data)\n- **China-sales scrutiny continues to shadow Surge AI, Mercor, and Turing.** Forbes' investigation (Surge courting Chinese labs, ~2% of Mercor's Q2 revenue from China, internal docs tying Turing to ByteDance) is still rippling through lab procurement conversations — expect tighter data-provenance and customer-disclosure clauses in new contracts. [Forbes](https://www.forbes.com/sites/annatong/2026/08/05/silicon-valleys-other-china-problem-its-training-their-ai/)\n- **Google outbid Mercor ($10M vs $7.5M) at auction for Spirit Airlines' de-identified enterprise data.** First public price signal for company operational data as a standalone AI asset — a new sourcing category worth watching for anyone in data supply. [TechBuzz](https://www.techbuzz.ai/articles/meet-the-billionaires-selling-ai-its-training-data)\n\n## New projects & opportunities\n\n- **IndiaAI Mission AI-CoE tender for strategic implementation partners closes today (Aug 25).** Government AI Centre-of-Excellence work is a direct channel into IndiaAI's dataset and data-labs agenda (500+ planned data labs); related empanelments continue on the IndiaAI portal. [TenderDetail](https://www.tenderdetail.com/Indian-tender/artificial-intelligence-tenders), [IndiaAI](https://indiaai.gov.in/article/meity-accelerates-empanelment-of-agencies-to-provide-ai-compute-and-services-for-the-indiaai-mission)\n- **Science-reproduction agents are becoming a product category — and a data demand driver.** London's Inherent (DeepMind alumni, $50M seed, out of stealth Aug 22) claims its Faraday agent beats Claude and GPT-5.5 at reproducing published papers. Building and grading such agents needs expert scientific annotation, eval rubrics, and RL environments — a fit for India's deep STEM talent pool. [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/22/inherent-founded-by-deepmind-alumni-says-its-ai-teammate-just-outperformed-anthropic-and-openai-at-replicating-research/)\n\n## Frontier lab movements\n\n- **Anthropic reportedly accelerating toward a $2T October IPO, filing possibly by late August.** Backers project $100–120B annualized revenue by year-end (vs $47B in May). A public, cash-rich Anthropic sustains one of the largest RLHF/eval data budgets in the market. [Fortune](https://fortune.com/2026/08/13/anthropic-ipo-2-trillion-october-largest-ever-spacex/), [Quartz](https://qz.com/anthropic-ipo-2-trillion-valuation-october-081326)\n- **Anthropic hired Google TPU founder Amir Salek as Broadcom seeks $60B+ in debt to lease it custom chips.** Massive compute lock-in (20 GW targeted by 2028) is a leading indicator of training-run scale — and of the human-data volumes needed to feed it. [Outlook Business](https://www.outlookbusiness.com/corporate/anthropic-eyes-its-own-ai-chips-why-it-hired-a-google-chip-veteran), [TNW](https://thenextweb.com/news/broadcom-60bn-ai-chip-debt-anthropic)\n- **Post-training is where the gains are: Zhipu's GLM-5.3 improved 50% on coding with zero architecture change, and its unreleased successor (\"Ox Alpha\") was fingerprinted on OpenRouter Aug 21.** Chinese labs squeezing capability out of post-training rather than bigger pretraining runs means growing demand for high-quality SFT/RLHF and agentic-environment data. [Unite.ai](https://www.unite.ai/z-ai-launches-glm-5-3-with-frontier-coding-and-a-cyber-capability-that-outgrew-its-training/), [CryptoBriefing](https://cryptobriefing.com/ox-alpha-stealth-ai-model-1m-context/)\n- **Price war intensifies: OpenAI cut GPT-5.6 Sol >20% (Aug 21); Anthropic froze Sonnet 5 pricing, canceling a planned Sept 1 hike; Alibaba raised $10.2B in Hong Kong (Aug 23) for full-stack AI.** Margin pressure at the labs eventually flows into vendor rate negotiations — plan pricing accordingly. [OpenAI](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.6-sol), [Releasebot/Anthropic](https://releasebot.io/updates/anthropic/claude-developer-platform), [Nikkei Asia](https://asia.nikkei.com/business/technology/alibaba-to-raise-10bn-via-new-hong-kong-shares-to-fund-ai-investments)\n\n## Research papers\n\n- **Prime Intellect's \"NanoGPT Speedrun Frontier\" (Aug 23): 18 frontier models autonomously optimized training code; Claude Fable 5 closed 82% of the gap to the human record.** Evidence that models can increasingly automate ML-engineering work — and a template for the agentic, verifiable eval harnesses labs now pay for. All 153 run traces are public. [Prime Intellect](https://www.primeintellect.ai/research/nanogpt-speedrun)\n- **Nvidia's AVO agent scored a perfect 100 on ARC-AGI-3 (all 183 levels) via scaffolding — memory, stuck-detection, hypothesis loops — not a bigger model.** Reinforces that agent harnesses and interactive RL environments, not just labeled datasets, are the next high-value data product for vendors to build. [Nvidia Developer Blog](https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/nvidia-avo-reaches-100-on-arc-agi-3-demonstrating-a-frontier-level-general-purpose-architecture-for-long-horizon-autonomous-agents/)\n\n## Leadership movements\n\n- **Amir Salek (founder of Google's TPU program, ex-Cerberus) joined Anthropic's compute team under James Bradbury.** Signals a multi-year custom-silicon push; watch for downstream inference-cost drops that make heavier eval/data pipelines economical. [Outlook Business](https://www.outlookbusiness.com/corporate/anthropic-eyes-its-own-ai-chips-why-it-hired-a-google-chip-veteran)\n- **Edward Hughes (ex-Google DeepMind) surfaced as chief scientist of Inherent, out of stealth Aug 22 with $50M.** Another senior DeepMind departure into an agent startup — the alumni diaspora keeps creating new, smaller data buyers beyond the big labs. [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/22/inherent-founded-by-deepmind-alumni-says-its-ai-teammate-just-outperformed-anthropic-and-openai-at-replicating-research/)\n"
